{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>Why should I be bereaved.</b> I would be bereft of both of you. One who buries his children is called שַׁכּוּל, and so regarding Jacob it says: ״כַּאֲשֶׁר שָׁכֹלְתִּי שָׁכָלְתִּי״." "<b>Both of you.</b> If he rises against you and you kill him, his sons will stand and kill you; and the holy spirit was infused in her and she prophesied that on one day they would die, as is explained in the chapter 'The one who is jealous of his wife'."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:52.559843611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}